WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.380
Instructor!

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.210
Did something happen?

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.950
Just get in.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.540
Yes, Sir.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.160
Nataru...

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.390
You know, my dad was always drinking.
He'd start in the afternoon.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:57.890
And he'd hit me at the drop of a hat.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.230
When he was in a bad mood, he'd hit me,

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.900
and when he was in a good mood he'd still hit me.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:07.170
It makes me sick to think I'm
related to a bastard like that.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.400
What are you trying to say?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.750
Your dad was pretty amazing, huh?

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.920
I hear he killed <i>twenty-five</i> government bigwigs.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.850
All by himself!

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:28.020
They even called him the Blue Fang.
I can't believe he'd leave the group!

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.630
It was for you, Nataru!

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.620
For you, the reject!

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.770
"Let All Our Hearts Be One!"

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.180
"Yakisoba!"

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.120
"Yakisoba Tools for Class 3-5"

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:08.500
"The Energetic Refugees"

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.170
Don't you think this photo would be better?

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.130
Okay. We'll use this, then.
"The Energetic Refugees"

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:12.300
No, no, that's no good!
"The Energetic Refugees"

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.200
No, no, that's no good!

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.670
Again?! You do this, then!

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.510
No. It's your job, Hazawa.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.150
Sheesh...

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.680
Dammit, why do I have to do this?!

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.480
Gah, I got glue on my hand!

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.480
What are you <i>doing?</i>

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.690
The paste is sticking out!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.090
This is such a pain in the ass!

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.490
How about this?

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.890
Ugh! Rejected.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.160
What?!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.490
I'm going out for a second.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.600
You trying to slack off?!

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:40.860
You ain't gettin' away.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.200
I'll be right back.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.070
You get back here fast, Senkawa!

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.410
What do you think of this, Hayamiya?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.240
Yeah, that's the way.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.690
"Let Our Hearts Be One"

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:08.680
"Shion Love"

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.230
Birdy...

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.100
You haven't said a word since this morning!

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.090
You've got Nataru on your mind, right?

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:26.040
He was sure acting kind of weird...

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.380
Don't you think, Birdy?

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.050
There's a chance you may be attacked.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.450
Huh?

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.420
What did he mean, attacked?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.950
Could he mean by aliens?

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.990
It seems impossible...

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.390
but what if Nataru's involved
in the streak of murders?

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.790
Impossible. No way.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:04.300
Someone your age shouldn't be sleeping this late!

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.990
I'm sorry.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.690
Get a grip.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.420
Eat this.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.250
Thank you.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.000
What happened, Nataru?

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.710
Good grief, the silent treatment again?

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.280
I really owe your dad a lot.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.350
Back when I was a student...

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:41.350
I remember I went to sell him books
whenever I was hard up for cash.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.490
He sold me the ones I wanted to read cheap.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.460
But the one thing he'd never
buy was my college textbooks.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:54.000
He'd say, "You need those right now."

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.570
And then his son collapsed in the
street for some mysterious reason.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.000
I couldn't just ignore you.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:30.600
Honestly, what in the world are you doing?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.900
Can't you even carry tea?

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.540
l-I'm sorry.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:39.580
Well, I kindly found the perfect job for you.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:45.850
Producer Ochikoshi said he
wanted to debut a "girls' unit."

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:48.040
Here. That's your costume.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.720
Looks pretty good on you.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.590
You're gonna dance and sing in that.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:58.230
A-Anything but that!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.800
No, you're going to make a lot of money doing it.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:04.930
For heaven's sake, anything but that! Please!

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:09.470
Shut up. There's no such thing as a free lunch.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.910
Hmm? I have an email...

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:19.080
"Miss Capella Titis, we have
set a date for our ruling

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.050
on your breach of military regulations.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:25.250
Therefore, you must present yourself
to the Federation Military Court

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.250
before your court date."

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:38.000
Capella Titis, I am Federation
investigator Kashu Geeze.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.640
Federation investigator?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:45.410
Well, now, do you actually think
I'm going to just let you catch me?

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.980
Maybe I'll kill you and run.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:51.910
I won't guarantee your life if you resist.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.920
I see.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.110
Then...

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.650
...let's test this.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.690
I'll tear you to pieces...

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:07.360
...Kashu Geeze.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.990
Stop it!

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:11.800
You hag!

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.500
Cape, you're not that kind of girl!

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:17.440
You're clumsy, inefficient, and unrefined,

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:21.840
but you're not someone who could
do a terrible thing like kill a person!

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.840
The truth is you're kind at heart...

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.620
I'll be waiting for you to come home.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.890
Come on back here when
you've finished doing your time.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.330
Ms. Irma...

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.330
Thank you for all you've
done for me. I won't forget it.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.740
One more <i>thing:</i>

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:54.140
could you please give a message
to investigator Birdy Cephon Altira?

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.310
Sure.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:58.910
Tell her that her request for
reinforcements has been approved.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.250
It's probably too late for them to do any good.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.750
As much red tape to cut through as ever, eh?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.190
Yes. Well, then...

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:11.490
Can I ask you one thing? How did you track me down?

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.930
Oh, that.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:15.400
I reported you.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.700
It's okay. I'll be a character witness for you.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.670
You old hag! I'll kill you!

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:25.070
I was almost <i>touched</i> back there!

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:30.280
Now, then... How about a cup of tea?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.020
That's it, I take it?

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:42.790
Yes. We'll finish this quickly.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.630
A fight with these savages
isn't even interesting, is it?

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.600
Who's there?!

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.570
Intruders!

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:20.890
Fire!

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:37.580
A primitive weapon. But it will
be enough for this operation.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:41.650
We can really kill them with this, right Colonel?

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:46.960
If we botch this, we'll be goners.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.530
Are lxiorans that frightening?

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:55.430
No... but I flatly refuse to let one of them kill me.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:57.830
Not one of those monsters!

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.870
Is that you, Tasera?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:04.610
It was you guys who made
that attack on Yokosuka, wasn't it?

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:05.980
Yes.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:10.050
We haven't received any information
from the Americans yet, but...

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:13.150
Your methods are too cruel.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:16.320
Stop harming the people of this planet.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:21.960
"People"? You've really
started supporting the natives.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:26.830
Leave me alone from now on.
I'll forget about you, too.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.960
I want to live quietly on this planet.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.870
Looking like that?

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.860
You mean to spend your whole
life pretending to be an Earthling?

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.540
Yes.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:42.680
I won't contact you again. Goodbye.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:43.870
Tasera!

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.260
What's wrong, Lamia?

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:01.600
You were lonely, huh?

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:07.440
The doctor said she remembers
the disaster when she's alone.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:10.770
Ah, that's right. Sorry, Lamia.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:14.880
I'm sure if you stay with us,
you'll grow able to talk again.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.280
We'll always be together from now on, okay?

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:22.420
Rejected!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.690
Why?! Why isn't there any space to display our

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:24.880
"Urban Legend Discovered!!!"
Why?! Why isn't there any space to display our

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:25.890
Why?! Why isn't there any space to display our

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.760
"Urban <i>Legend:</i> Investigate
the Old Lady in Sandals!"?!

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.960
We don't need to display stupid stuff like that!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.130
What do you mean, "stupid"?!

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:38.400
Totally rejected! We're in the final
sprint on our refugee camp article!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:43.740
Oh, hey. EBC did a report on
the Roppongi Ruins recently, right?

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.770
They might have some good photos.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:48.740
Okay, one sec.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.550
It's on their homepage, Kitamura.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:53.120
Hey, you're right!

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.110
There's a lot of pics.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.120
H-Hey, time out!

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:00.460
What's with you?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.730
Sorry, but I want to take a look at this one.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.120
This is...

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.280
That's Nataru's...

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:51.870
Faroid was killed here.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.880
Aren't you going to look for Nataru?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.190
That's Nataru's, right?

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.440
It can't have been Nataru!

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:01.430
I haven't said anything yet.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:06.910
An Altan couldn't kill a Gient like that.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:15.190
Then Nataru isn't the perp!
It's decided! Thank goodness!

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.130
"202 Shion Arita"

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.130
"6 Transmit via infrared"

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.900
"Send one address book entry? Yes / No"

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.590
"Connecting via infrared"

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.210
I'm going to do a bit of shopping.

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:32.040
See you soon.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.900
I'm pathetic.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:07.170
Huh, he takes pretty good pictures.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:13.510
I'm sick of convenience store dinners...

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.750
Nataru!

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.740
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.530
Nataru...

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.490
Man, doesn't look like the
rain will quit anytime soon.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:42.010
Hello?

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.150
Miss Arita?

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:48.450
Sorry, but I dug up your cell phone number.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:50.650
It's rude to just call me out of the blue, yessiree.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:53.290
I am sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:56.330
I don't feel like talking to you right now, Sir.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:17:01.230
Don't hang up! This is about Nataru Shinmyou.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.830
You've seen Nataru?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.370
Yeah, he was staying with me up until yesterday.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.370
What?

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.870
But the jerk left.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:11.070
What does this mean?

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:14.340
He's in no shape to wander around.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.650
He wasn't in his apartment or the bookstore.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:21.650
Do you know where he might go?

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:24.190
I'm coming over there right now.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.180
Huh? W-Wait, what about school?

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:35.190
That was fast!

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:41.070
Hey, at least take off your shoes.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.780
<i>Nataru...</i>

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:50.050
Sheesh, you're so violent.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.040
When did he leave?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.120
On my way back from the
convenience store last night,

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.520
he flew out of here right in front of my eyes.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:02.720
And he messed up my photos and materials, too.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.390
Where is that stuff now?!

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.230
U-Uh, over there...

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.960
Hey, what happened to Nataru?!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.100
Tasera...

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:17.940
You know something, don't you?

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:20.080
Where did you take this picture?

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:20.810
Huh?

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.380
Where?!

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:25.370
At an orphanage, Contact Garden.

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:32.150
Oh, yes, that's Lamia Tase.

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.290
Where is she?

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.920
She's not here anymore.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:41.130
She was fortunate enough to
gain a new mother and father.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.120
Where are they?!

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:50.670
There are so many children here who
lost their parents to the strange light,

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:53.780
so why does everyone focus on her, I wonder?

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.680
Pardon?

00:18:55.680 --> 00:19:02.310
Ah, you see, someone else just
asked me where Lamia went, too.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.180
No...

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.210
No!

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:08.680
You damn brat! It pisses me off just looking at you!

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:15.480
How long is it gonna rain?

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.160
Tasera?

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:23.570
I thought you weren't going
to contact us anymore?

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.540
You'll be last.

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:30.270
There are three left. I'll kill you last.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:34.510
You just quake in your boots until then.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:35.500
Nataru...

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:07.380
I was looking for that.
I wondered where I'd lost it.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.370
I'll kill every last one.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:32.660
Why...

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:39.160
Why didn't you arrest him?!
You're a Federation investigator!

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:17.340
<i>Birdy found out that Nataru was</i>
<i>behind the murders of the escapees.</i>

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:20.610
<i>However, Birdy agonized over this truth,</i>

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:24.580
<i>and became irritated with</i>
<i>herself as an investigator.</i>

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:28.420
<i>Nataru's body was reaching</i>
<i>the limits of exhaustion,</i>

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:31.410
<i>but he continued his quest for vengeance.</i>

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:36.280
<i>Please, Nataru, one more time...</i>
